 co-working environment: come hang out and chat, work on your own, seek help, make friends. Or, a little bit of everything! Check out our <a href=\"https://d-rug.github.io/\" style=\"font-size:1rem;border-color:rgb(66,133,244)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://d-rug.github.io/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465145804000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3YUdXI_5krGxwAsXdkrACa\">website</a> for more information.</div><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"border-color:rgb(49,49,49)\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"font-size:1rem;border-color:rgb(49,49,49)\"><b style=\"font-size:1rem;border-color:rgb(49,49,49)\">We are also seeking presenters!</b> It is nice to mix things up with occasional presentations. In the past, we&#39;ve had (15- to 45-minute) presentations ranging from data types, to tidyverse tools, to spatial data, to the Google Earth Engine plugin for R. If you would like to hone your teaching, need an excuse to perfect your cRaft, or want to show off a cool R trick you learned, shoot us an email and we can add your presentation to our <a href=\"https://d-rug.github.io/calendar.html\" style=\"font-size:1rem;border-color:rgb(66,133,244)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://d-rug.github.io/calendar.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465145804000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1XJi2zwP0_88njjRXX-IhL\">calendar</a>! Presentations can be in-person or virtual (and in-person presentations will be streamed for virtual attendees).</div></div></div>"
